From 37ddc42aee86ebc38d8f0e306b0a2bcaf47c9bd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hanbang <hanbang@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:54:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Libretro: run a frame line by line (hb_ws_* API) for a
 two-console frontend

Split Emulate() and retro_run() into run_pre (options, input,
frameskip) / emu_begin / emu_line (one 256-cycle scanline) / emu_end /
run_post (video and audio out). retro_run() simply calls them in order,
so the single-console core behaves exactly as before. A frontend that
hosts two consoles alternates emu_line() between them and passes
finished serial bytes across with hb_ws_link_take()/hb_ws_link_give().

Also exported: hb_ws_set_render (skip drawing for the hidden console),
hb_ws_framebuffer, hb_ws_internal_eeprom, and test-only helpers
hb_ws_trace, hb_ws_watch (physical write watchpoint), hb_ws_cpu_reg.
link.T exports hb_ws_* next to retro_*.

---
 libretro.c                    | 182 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 link.T                        |   2 +-
 mednafen/wswan/eeprom.c       |   6 ++
 mednafen/wswan/eeprom.h       |   1 +
 mednafen/wswan/wswan-memory.c |   6 ++
 5 files changed, 163 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

